messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI assistants become standard in work and education.",
      "detail": "Agentic software handles routine analysis, drafting, and coding under human oversight. Productivity rises unevenly, prompting new training and safety practices."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "EVs reach roughly 40% of global new car sales.",
      "detail": "Battery costs and charging networks improve, and policy nudges accelerate adoption. Oil demand growth in transport slows markedly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2029,
      "event": "A major near-miss AI incident prompts global safety standards.",
      "detail": "An autonomous system cascades errors across a cyber-physical network before being contained. Governments and industry adopt incident reporting, red-teaming, and evaluation requirements."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Global fossil fuel demand peaks and begins sustained decline.",
      "detail": "Efficiency, electrification, and alternatives outcompete in most new applications. Investment tilts decisively toward clean generation and storage."
    },
    {
      "year": 2031,
      "event": "A new respiratory pandemic is contained far faster than COVID-19.",
      "detail": "mRNA and vector platforms deliver variant-matched vaccines within weeks, and global surveillance coordinates responses. Mortality and economic damage are significantly reduced."
    },
    {
      "year": 2033,
      "event": "The first country runs a year of 24/7 carbon‑free electricity across all seasons.",
      "detail": "A mix of nuclear, hydro, geothermal, long-duration storage, and HVDC balancing proves the model. Replication plans spread to other regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "A grid‑connected fusion demonstration delivers sustained net electricity.",
      "detail": "It operates for hours to days at meaningful power, validating engineering pathways. Pilot commercial plants are funded, though scaling remains a decade‑plus effort."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Global warming reaches about 1.7°C above preindustrial levels.",
      "detail": "Heat extremes, fires, and floods intensify, pushing large adaptation programs. Crop mixes and water systems shift measurably across continents."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "Quantum and AI co-design become routine for targeted drugs and materials.",
      "detail": "For specific classes of chemistry, simulation narrows candidates dramatically before lab work. Development cycles shorten and costs drop."
    },
    {
      "year": 2044,
      "event": "A severe geomagnetic storm disrupts power and satellites for weeks in some regions.",
      "detail": "Blackouts and navigation outages spur grid hardening, satellite shielding, and emergency comms upgrades. Space weather forecasting becomes a mainstream resilience tool."
    },
    {
      "year": 2047,
      "event": "An international AI governance treaty is adopted.",
      "detail": "It mandates model evaluations, compute and chip export tracking, and incident disclosure, with third‑party audits. Most nations implement risk‑tiered controls while preserving research channels."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Coastal adaptation protects most megacities while managed retreat begins in deltas.",
      "detail": "Defenses, surge barriers, and nature‑based solutions buy time, but low‑lying communities relocate. Insurance, zoning, and public finance are retooled."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Global median life expectancy exceeds 80 years.",
      "detail": "Preventive genomics, continuous monitoring, and early‑intervention care reduce cardiovascular, infectious, and some cancer burdens. Gains remain uneven across regions but narrow."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "A permanent crewed lunar base with in‑situ resource use operates continuously.",
      "detail": "Local regolith processing provides water, oxygen, and building materials. The base supports science, telecom relays, and manufacturing experiments."
    },
    {
      "year": 2068,
      "event": "Net global greenhouse gas emissions fall below zero.",
      "detail": "Deep decarbonization is complemented by large‑scale carbon removal and ecosystem restoration under stricter governance. Temperatures begin to plateau with multi‑decade lags."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Global mean sea‑level rise passes 0.5 meters.",
      "detail": "Tens of millions have relocated, and coastal economies reconfigure. New ports and elevated districts become standard."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "A planetary‑defense mission deflects a hazardous near‑Earth object.",
      "detail": "A kinetic impactor and follow‑up gravity tractor adjust its trajectory safely. Continuous sky surveys and ready launch systems become standing infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Warming stabilizes near 2.1–2.3°C as emissions remain net‑negative.",
      "detail": "Impacts persist but become more predictable, and biodiversity corridors enable slow recovery in many regions. Food systems rely on climate‑resilient crops and controlled‑environment agriculture."
    },
    {
      "year": 2125,
      "event": "Mars hosts a rotating cohort of research settlers with partial local production.",
      "detail": "Fuel, oxygen, and water are produced on‑site; habitats rely on imported high‑tech components. Surface stays are measured in months to years."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Clean energy abundance reshapes economics worldwide.",
      "detail": "Advanced fission, fusion, and space‑linked solar with massive storage dominate. Desalination, recycling, and materials synthesis become cheap and ubiquitous."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Synthetic ecology and conservation engineering revive many ecosystems.",
      "detail": "Assisted migration and habitat re‑knitting expand rewilded zones. Some lost functions are restored using closely related or engineered species under careful oversight."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Fast interstellar probes return data from nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Beamed‑sail craft launched centuries earlier perform flybys and transmit high‑rate observations. Exoplanet atmospheres and system architectures are characterized in detail."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Large rotating space habitats house millions in cislunar space.",
      "detail": "Closed‑loop life support and asteroid‑sourced materials mature. Habitats specialize in research, industry, and culture."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Languages and cultures diversify while deep archives preserve continuity.",
      "detail": "Universal translation and rich historical records reduce fragmentation costs. Cultural lineages are traced and remixed with intent."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Elective bio‑cyber augmentation is widespread and rights‑protected.",
      "detail": "Neural interfaces, sensory extensions, and somatic gene edits are normalized. Legal frameworks maintain personhood across biological and digital embodiments."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Asteroid mining underpins megastructure‑scale construction in the solar system.",
      "detail": "Mass drivers and automated factories produce bulk materials for habitats and power arrays. Economies shift toward off‑Earth heavy industry."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Sea level stands 2–4 meters above 2000 levels and stabilizes.",
      "detail": "Ice sheet response slows, and coastal geographies settle into long‑term defenses and new urban forms. Marine ecosystems adapt around restored blue‑carbon habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "A high‑orbit solar power ring supplies most imported energy to Earth and habitats.",
      "detail": "Gigascale collectors beam power via tightly controlled microwaves and lasers with wide safety margins. Energy scarcity becomes rare."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Mars and several icy moons host self‑sufficient cities.",
      "detail": "Local agriculture, industry, and governance mature; trade focuses on designs and specialty goods. Terraforming remains partial and regional."
    },
    {
      "year": 5500,
      "event": "Global sea level reaches roughly 5–7 meters above 2000 levels.",
      "detail": "Final major relocations conclude, and new coastal ecologies and cities flourish. Cultural memory of earlier shorelines persists in archives and monuments."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "The first interstellar colony fleet departs with fusion/beam propulsion.",
      "detail": "A mix of generation, stasis, and AI‑caretaker architectures is used. Travel times are measured in centuries with robust redundancy."
    },
    {
      "year": 6500,
      "event": "An interstellar colony achieves full self‑sufficiency and demographic stability.",
      "detail": "Local industry, agriculture, medicine, and education decouple from supply from Earth. Distinct cultural identities and legal norms solidify."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Civilizational cycles occur without losing scientific‑technical continuity.",
      "detail": "Redundant institutions, off‑world archives, and automated education buffer downturns. Risk management and catastrophe insurance are embedded in governance."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "Long‑memory institutions regularly refresh core knowledge and language.",
      "detail": "Standard curricula, living libraries, and periodic reforms limit drift and fragmentation. Interoperability across habitats and polities is preserved."
    },
    {
      "year": 8500,
      "event": "Human‑descended cultures span the solar system and a handful of nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Interoperable law compacts and norms support peaceful coexistence despite distance. Diversity in biology and computation coexists under shared rights principles."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Interstellar trade stabilizes around information and rare physical couriers.",
      "detail": "Laser communications carry designs, culture, and science; high‑speed courier craft move compact, high‑value goods. Economies synchronize slowly by necessity."
    },
    {
      "year": 9500,
      "event": "Conservative climate stewardship becomes routine planetary management.",
      "detail": "Carbon cycle oversight, ecosystem buffering, and limited, reversible albedo control operate with strict guardrails. Key Earth system indicators remain within safe bands."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity persists as diverse biological and digital lineages linked across worlds.",
      "detail": "Identities and cultures vary widely, but core ethical and scientific traditions endure. Earth remains a thriving cradle and commons within a broader civilization."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity weathers a turbulent 21st and 22nd century, stabilizes climate near ~2°C, and builds resilient institutions that manage advanced technologies prudently. Over millennia, abundant clean energy and space industry enable off‑world habitats and a few interstellar outposts, while culture and biology diversify under rights frameworks. By year 10000, humans and their descendants remain, distributed and varied, with continuity of knowledge and stewardship of Earth."
}
